im]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]missing agent name.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]tribe_wait_reference_validation_and_display.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ak[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reject reserved tribe references in wait and fork targets[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]reserved-tribe-guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reserved-tribe-guard: add a canonical reserved-tribe concept to core and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reject `@default` (and any other reserved pseudo-tribe) wherever a tribe[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reference is used as a `%wait` or `#fork` target, so the launch fails [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with a clear message instead of parking forever.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared tribe wait binding resolver[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tribe-wait-binding[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tribe-wait-binding: extract the `tribe_candidate` ordering and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]aggregation rules into a pure, snapshot-driven resolver in Python core [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that both the wait index and the TUI can call, and add a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pending/bound/reserved classification the display layer can consume [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]without touching disk.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Tribe-aware wait rendering in the Agents tab[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ace-tribe-wait-display[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tribe-wait-binding[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ace-tribe-wait-display: stop classifying tribe wait targets as missing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent names, give them their own wait lane tag and tribe identity [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]styling, show the bound entity and its status once one exists, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]refresh the affected render-cache keys, help text, and PNG snapshots.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Surface waits that can never resolve[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]unresolvable-wait-surface[dim] · [dim][/dim]after reserved-tribe-guard, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]ace-tribe-wait-display[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]unresolvable-wait-surface: give already-parked reserved-tribe waits a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]distinct \"this wait can never resolve\" presentation in ACE so agents [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]launched before the guard landed are diagnosable rather than silently [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pending.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ak","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","phase_bead_id":"sase-ak.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-42396f1942682519dce24264932ebf03","started_at":"2026-07-28T21:06:45.551738+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785273824,"sha":"21e75272f628e4ce84bfe55453f2cb5fe55950e4","subject":"feat: add snapshot-driven tribe wait binding resolver"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"1e6d5fc67bf2a530f7f994e6578db038cc3987f5dd827dcbd4087e3e0dca051f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ak.2/chat.md","size_bytes":5278},"commits":{"digest":"90b074c6a0c5f6e76f7a54f504c3b82693722a95d885877f5c631845c38cd0ab","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ak.2/commits.json","size_bytes":231},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ak.2/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"3ddd9f07ad76f06